diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 8fe0a65..6c25ff3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -117,3 +117,54 @@ Options:
   --version                   Version number.
   --configure                 Read an ini file.
 ```
+
+### Native AGC input (optional)
+
+Build the MIT-licensed [AGC library](https://github.com/refresh-bio/agc)
+(`make libagc`), then configure PFP++ with
+`-DPFP_ENABLE_AGC=ON -DAGC_ROOT=/path/to/agc`. This adapter uses AGC's
+collection/segment C++ interface; the tested revision is
+`e67e3fc865a459779118d3d4e9fbdf42c70ba75e` (3.2), with archive format 3.
+AGC is optional and is neither downloaded nor linked in a default build.
+An enabled build requires C++20 and OpenMP.
+
+```
+pfp++ -t collection.agc --agc -o collection -j 16 -w 10 -p 100
+```
+
+`--agc` explicitly selects the archive. The logical text consists of each
+contig reversed (not reverse complemented), uppercased, and followed by
+byte `0x1e`, including the final contig. Samples and contigs retain their
+archive-internal order. `--agc-names PATH` optionally writes
+`contig<TAB>total-1-stream_offset-length<TAB>length` metadata, matching
+`agc2flat --revlines --upper --sep 1e`.
+
+The upstream `-t` parser in this revision is serial; it has no file chunk
+partitioning or parallel overlap algorithm. File/gzip/FIFO behavior stays
+unchanged. In AGC mode `-j` (1..96) controls independent decoder sessions
+that seek and fetch 1 MiB regions in parallel. The parser consumes their
+results in order. Its rolling hash and last `w` phrase bytes persist across
+chunk boundaries, so chunks need no extra overlap and introduce no new
+phrase boundaries. This is parallel archive input, not parallel phrase
+construction.
+
+No FUSE mount, child extractor, pipe, or extracted text file is used by the
+AGC reader. Metadata is indexed once. Segment lengths are counted from
+compressed delta instructions, without expanding matches or N runs; this
+also handles metadata/decoded-length discrepancies in existing archives.
+The index is proportional to archive descriptors and compressed packs,
+not expanded collection length. Each decoder owns its archive handle and
+ZSTD context. There is no persistent decoded sequence cache; the delivery
+buffer is at most `j` MiB, plus metadata and each active segment/pack.
+Reference and uncompressed pack sizes above 256 MiB are rejected. Archive
+input must remain unchanged during a run. Invalid ranges and decoder
+length disagreements fail the operation.
+
+`pfp_source_probe` is an enabled-build test/benchmark utility. For example,
+`pfp_source_probe agc collection.agc 16 0 100000000` hashes a 100 MB range
+and reports initialization time and steady read throughput separately.
+The `file` mode is the same control with a regular extracted file. The
+optional `emit` argument writes the requested bytes for differential tests.
+Run `tests/test_agc.py --pfp build/pfp++ --probe build/pfp_source_probe
+--agc /path/to/agc --agc2flat /path/to/agc2flat` for parse/dictionary,
+names, seek, separator, and error regressions.
